Package: NADIA
Type: Package
Title: Missing Value-Aware Differential Expression Analysis of DIA Proteomics Data
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R: person(
    given = "Sergio",
    family = "Ciordia",
    email = "sciordia@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides a complete workflow for the differential expression
    analysis of protein quantification data, with particular attention to the
    missing values that dominate data-independent acquisition (DIA) experiments.
    Raw reports from Spectronaut, DIA-NN and Proteome Discoverer (both TMT and
    label-free) are parsed into a common structure and then normalised,
    optionally batch-corrected, imputed and tested for differential abundance
    with limma or limpa. Thirteen normalisation methods and nineteen imputation
    methods are available, including two-stage hybrids that treat values missing
    at random and missing not at random separately. Benchmarking functions score
    and rank method combinations using ground-truth simulation and spike-in
    datasets, so that a choice of pipeline can be justified on the data at hand
    rather than by convention. Results are summarised as interactive Highcharts
    figures, static ggplot2 and ComplexHeatmap graphics, and sortable tables.
